In article <1991Jun30.015129.11892@cs.mcgill.ca> storm@cs.mcgill.ca (Marc WANDSCHNEIDER) writes:
>I have been playing nethack quite frequently lately in my spare time, and
>it's beginning to bother me.
>It seems that as soon as I start doing well, the game decides to send some 10
>or twelve Killer Bees/Hill Orcs/Mordor Orcs/Fire Ants/Bugbears/etc after me.
>Now a player has only so many Hit Point, a Wand of Big Zaps does too, and a
>TurnedintoVAMPIREpet can only attack so many enemies at the same time.
>Could somebody please give me SOME sort of suggestion as to how I can go 
>about avoiding getting wasted every time I start doing well...?
<SPOILER>
1) Back up until you are in a corridor, then you'll only have to fight
   with one monster at the time.
2) Go to the down or up stairs and when you are low on your hitpoints just
   go down or upstairs to recover. Be carefull that on this new level you
   don't run into the same problem.
In both cases you can get a temporary relief by writing the 'E'-word (oeps
you wanted the full word: Elbereth) on the ground. In a corridor this is
very successfull when you write it, put on a ring of levitation and float 
away. In this case the monsters can't even tail you. Note that walking away
destroys what you have written.
